{%- comment -%}
  Customization Philosophy
  Render with: {% render 'customization-philosophy' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="o4-customization-philosophy" aria-label="Customization philosophy">
  <style>
    .o4-customization-philosophy {
      --o4-custom-ink: #e8f6ff;
      --o4-custom-ink-soft: rgba(200, 224, 255, 0.72);
      --o4-custom-accent: #43e7ff;
      --o4-custom-line: rgba(140, 210, 255, 0.24);
      --o4-custom-panel: rgba(7, 12, 24, 0.8);
      color: var(--o4-custom-ink);
      font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 48px auto;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__inner {
      max-width: 1100px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 16px;
      display: grid;
      gap: 22px;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__head {
      display: grid;
      gap: 10px;
      text-align: left;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__eyebrow {
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.24em;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      color: var(--o4-custom-accent);
      font-family: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__title {
      font-family: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
      font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.2vw, 2.2rem);
      margin: 0;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__lead {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--o4-custom-ink-soft);
      line-height: 1.7;
      max-width: 820px;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: 18px;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__card {
      background: var(--o4-custom-panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--o4-custom-line);
      border-radius: 18px;
      padding: 16px 18px;
      display: grid;
      gap: 10px;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__card h3 {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--o4-custom-accent);
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__card h4 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: rgba(232, 246, 255, 0.85);
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__card ul,
    .o4-customization-philosophy__card ol {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 18px;
      color: var(--o4-custom-ink-soft);
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__card li {
      margin: 0.25rem 0;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__callout {
      background: rgba(10, 16, 28, 0.9);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 14px 18px;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: rgba(230, 250, 255, 0.88);
      text-align: center;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-size: 0.92rem;
      background: var(--o4-custom-panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--o4-custom-line);
      border-radius: 14px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__table th,
    .o4-customization-philosophy__table td {
      padding: 12px 14px;
      text-align: left;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
      color: var(--o4-custom-ink-soft);
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__table th {
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      color: var(--o4-custom-accent);
      background: rgba(8, 14, 26, 0.75);
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__table tr:last-child td {
      border-bottom: none;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__footer {
      background: rgba(8, 12, 22, 0.92);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
      border-radius: 18px;
      padding: 16px 18px;
      display: grid;
      gap: 10px;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__footer h3 {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--o4-custom-accent);
    }

    .o4-customization-philosophy__footer ul {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 18px;
      color: var(--o4-custom-ink-soft);
    }

    body.mode-minimal .o4-customization-philosophy__card,
    body.mode-minimal .o4-customization-philosophy__table,
    body.mode-minimal .o4-customization-philosophy__footer,
    body.mode-minimal .o4-customization-philosophy__callout {
      background: rgba(10, 14, 22, 0.96);
      box-shadow: none;
    }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .o4-customization-philosophy {
        margin: 32px auto;
      }
      .o4-customization-philosophy__table th,
      .o4-customization-philosophy__table td {
        padding: 10px 12px;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="o4-customization-philosophy__inner">
    <div class="o4-customization-philosophy__head">
      <p class="o4-customization-philosophy__eyebrow">Customization philosophy</p>
      <h2 class="o4-customization-philosophy__title">Use one product page in most cases</h2>
      <p class="o4-customization-philosophy__lead">
        Default recommendation: one product page with a Customization Method selector (None / Sublimation / Vinyl).
        The long answer below explains when to keep one page vs when to split, and how it works operationally.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="o4-customization-philosophy__grid">
      <article class="o4-customization-philosophy__card">
        <h3>Why this is usually correct</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>It is the same base product (SKU, fit, material, use case).</li>
          <li>Customers compare methods while deciding, not before.</li>
          <li>Better SEO (one strong page instead of diluted traffic).</li>
          <li>Less catalog and inventory complexity.</li>
          <li>Easier upsells and mixed-method orders.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="o4-customization-philosophy__card">
        <h3>How the same page behaves</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Customer lands on product page.</li>
          <li>Selects size and color (base product).</li>
          <li>Selects Customization Method.</li>
          <li>Sublimation -> shows sublimation-only options and timeline.</li>
          <li>Vinyl -> shows vinyl-only options and timeline.</li>
          <li>Price and delivery estimate update dynamically.</li>
        </ol>
        <h4>Cart receives</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Base SKU.</li>
          <li>Customization method(s).</li>
          <li>Placement(s).</li>
          <li>Artwork files.</li>
          <li>Production rules.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="o4-customization-philosophy__card">
        <h3>When to use separate pages</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>The finished product is meaningfully different (all-over vs logo-only).</li>
          <li>Pricing logic is fundamentally different and too complex for one UI.</li>
          <li>Marketing or SEO demands method-specific funnels.</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <article class="o4-customization-philosophy__card">
        <h3>Hybrid best practice</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Main page: /products/custom-shirt</li>
          <li>Method entries: /products/custom-shirt?method=sublimation</li>
          <li>Method entries: /products/custom-shirt?method=vinyl</li>
          <li>Preselect method and update hero copy, same backend logic.</li>
          <li>Clean UX, clean ops, strong SEO.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="o4-customization-philosophy__card">
        <h3>Backend and operational model</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Base product: SKU SHIRT-BASE-001.</li>
          <li>Customization line items: SUB-FRONT, SUB-BACK, VINYL-1C-FRONT, VINYL-2C-SLEEVE.</li>
          <li>Production flags: proof required, additional days, mixed-method indicator.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="o4-customization-philosophy__callout">
      From the customer's point of view: "Same product, different ways to customize."
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3 class="o4-customization-philosophy__eyebrow">Decision table (quick)</h3>
      <table class="o4-customization-philosophy__table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Scenario</th>
            <th>One page</th>
            <th>Separate pages</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Same garment</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>No</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Different visual result</td>
            <td>No</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Same SKU</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>No</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Different buyer intent</td>
            <td>No</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Complex pricing but manageable</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>No</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>SEO-driven campaigns</td>
            <td>Hybrid</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="o4-customization-philosophy__footer">
      <h3>Final recommendation for sublimation and vinyl</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Start with one product page using a Customization Method selector.</li>
        <li>Use dynamic pricing and a dynamic production timeline.</li>
        <li>Move to separate pages only after you see user confusion or need targeted marketing funnels.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
